10. She references being unable to yawn or pout in text commands, indicating these are known traits or quirks associated with her persona. (Verbatim: "i'm not freeing the yawn no no no no... now i'll just just break yay skittles arigato.") [end of text]



1. She is grumpy when waking up and prefers to sleep in. (Verbatim: "i'm quite grumpy here it'll be like they got earlier i'm like no five more minutes yeah so yeah naps naps city naps are the way")

2. She enjoys napping and considers naps highly important. (Verbatim: "naps naps city naps are the way naps supremacy yeah let's have our naps")

3. She grew up with two cats, one of which was particularly attached to her. (Verbatim: "i grew up with a cat and my cat i grew up with two cats and my the one that was more like my cat was always always always making noise in the night")

4. Her childhood cat used to wake her up at night by making noise and once sat on her head. (Verbatim: "my cat used to sit on my head too um but i wouldn't wake up my cat would try to wake me up")

5. Her cat used to hunt and bring live animals, especially baby sparrows, to her doorstep. (Verbatim: "the most common animal my cat used to bring in would be a baby sparrow yeah we had a lot of sparrows where i lived")

6. She once rescued an injured baby blackbird and went to great lengths to find a local charity that would take it in. (Verbatim: "i put it in a little shoebox with some bread and then i tried to call up different places to be like hello i have injured bird is for you")

7. She dislikes using the phone and finds it terrifying. (Verbatim: "i don't like using the phone as as we know using the phone is terrifying")

8. She used to keep spiders in the house as a child and wasn’t afraid of them until influenced by classmates. (Verbatim: "i used to not be scared of spiders at all and then i remember when i went to school and all the other girls in my class were like freaking out over spiders")

9. She is specifically afraid of spiders with thick legs, which she calls "chunky boy spiders," but is okay with thin-legged ones. (Verbatim: "if they're um it's because we the wait let me show you we have um most of our spiders here look like this... but when their legs are thick then then then i um then i worry")

10. She grew up in an old house with a unique ceiling material that made noise when daddy long legs walked on it, which used to stress her out. (Verbatim: "we had this like really awful flammable material on the ceiling that needed removing... it was really loud when the daddy long legs would like like land on it so I could hear them in the night") [end of text]



1. She grew up in England and refers to British English terms, such as calling ladybugs "ladybirds." (Verbatim: "we don't call them ladybugs here in england okay we don't call them ladybugs here")

2. She had a childhood desire for a pet, which she fulfilled temporarily by keeping a ladybird as a pet. (Verbatim: "i really wanted i really wanted a pet so i got myself a pet i call myself a lady bird")

3. As a child, she kept a ladybird in an airtight see-through container with a plastic leaf, not knowing it needed real food and air. (Verbatim: "i put it in this airtight see-through box... i chopped off the plastic leaf and then i put that in the box")

4. She experienced sadness and guilt as a child when her pet ladybird died, believing she had failed as a caretaker. (Verbatim: "absolute shock horror what how did it die... i was such a good ladybird mother what what")

5. Her family moved to a second home during her childhood where they had a garage-like outbuilding that became a seasonal nesting site for ladybirds. (Verbatim: "in the second home um we had this like garage thing... the whole ceiling inside this garage would become ladybirds")

6. The ladybirds stopped coming to the family’s outbuilding after the roof blew off during a windy day in England. (Verbatim: "one year the garage roof blew off on like a really windy day so i don't think they came back after that incident")

7. She has a strong dislike of winged insects, particularly those that are large and fly, such as crane flies (called daddy longlegs in the UK). (Verbatim: "it's got wings i don't like it when it's got wings okay it it's got wings we don't like it")

8. She recalls that children in her school used to cruelly catch daddy longlegs and rip off their legs, though she personally refused to participate. (Verbatim: "a lot of kids in school used to do this... rip off some of its legs... i didn't because i wasn't going near it")

9. She and her brothers used to collect wood lice (roly-polies) and play with them as children, considering it relatively harmless. (Verbatim: "me and my brothers would collect them and then just like play with them like because they're small balls")

10. She encountered a large ball of baby spiders near a garage and accidentally touched it, causing her parents to become very upset. (Verbatim: "gosh my parents were so mad they were so angry... i touched it") [end of text]



1. She has a fear of bugs being dangerous, stemming from a jungle trip where many bugs could harm her. (Verbatim: "when i was like in the jungle there's so many bugs that can hurt you i'm not used to it i'm just not used to it like i'm just not used to bugs being a thing")

2. She previously lived in or visited a jungle environment where she encountered many dangerous insects. (Verbatim: "when i was like in the jungle there's so many bugs that can hurt you... oh don't touch that that'll injure you don't touch that that'll hurt you i'll don't touch that i'll kill you")

3. She formed a bond with a pet black widow spider during her time in the jungle, which she considered a friend and protector. (Verbatim: "it was my pet black widow spider... it defended me from the other bugs it had a really really really strong web")

4. She is from England, where she notes bugs are generally harmless compared to other regions. (Verbatim: "i'm in england so it wasn't it wasn't the one in this picture... there's no reason to be afraid of bugs in england to be honest")

5. She strongly dislikes wasps, calling them "stupid angry angry angry bug[s] in the bin". (Verbatim: "unless it's wasps wasps can go in the bin stupid wasps stupid angry angry angry bug in the bin")

6. She hand-washed clothes while in the jungle, using a personal laundry line. (Verbatim: "each person had their own little like laundry line area because you always had to you know constantly well hand wash your clothes")

7. She used a stick to gently move a spider’s web out of the way while doing laundry, showing care for the creature. (Verbatim: "i got my stick my trusty old stick and basically just like moved the web and then like transferred the web to another part")

8. She took pictures and videos of her pet spider fighting other insects like a mantis and catching a cicada. (Verbatim: "i have one of it catching a cicada like i heckin got it fighting everything... i started taking pictures of it and videos of it")

9. She defended her pet spider from others who wanted to remove it, insisting it was useful and harmless to her. (Verbatim: "some people freaked out and they were like shouldn't and i was like no no i'm keeping this this spider gets rid of all the other scary bugs so i'm keeping it")

10. She expresses empathy toward people with fears and believes no one should be embarrassed of their fears. (Verbatim: "i don't think anyone should ever be embarrassed of their fears you know like a fear is just a human instinct to protect yourself") [end of text]



1. She has experience working as a coder and has worked at a workplace where her code was reviewed by others. (Verbatim: "i bet there's people at my old workplace looking through my absolute gibberish spaghetti code and is like did we just pay her to like write random thoughts")

2. She struggles emotionally with coding and often feels bad while doing it, even as an experienced developer. (Verbatim: "you could be a heckin senior developer and have been like you know coding for god knows how long and it's still gonna happen... that feeling never goes")

3. She leaves playful and encouraging comments in her code, often using emojis or messages to future readers. (Verbatim: "i leave a lot of cute comments... like dear future reader of this comment have a nice day")

4. She finds debugging code to be a painful and frustrating experience. (Verbatim: "debugging pain the bug the bug pain the bug pain honestly i have too many memories of just my head against my keyboard")

5. She believes that feeling incompetent while coding is universal and normal, even for experienced developers. (Verbatim: "that is how we all feel that is how we all feel all the time")

6. She discovered her passions by identifying activities that caused her the least mental discomfort while learning. (Verbatim: "it was more like things that didn't hurt my brain so much when i was learning about it that's how i discovered what i enjoy")

7. She finds studying or intense learning mentally exhausting, comparing it to putting her brain on a treadmill. (Verbatim: "studying always felt like putting my brain on a treadmill and i'd be so tired i'd be like i need a nap")

8. She is self-deprecating about her intelligence, joking that she frequently loses brain cells or is wrong. (Verbatim: "i didn't lose my brain cell you guys are just borrowing it... it's not always right well no it's usually wrong")

9. She enjoys editing, graphic design, and creative tasks, especially when time passes quickly while doing them. (Verbatim: "when i'm doing like editing or graphic design or anything... that is when time would pass really really really fast")

10. She embraces being wrong as part of learning and believes constant correctness is suspicious or unhealthy. (Verbatim: "i think it's good to be wrong because something's wrong if you're always right") [end of text]



1. She participated in poetry slams to overcome her social anxiety and communication difficulties. (Verbatim: "it was more like a thing to participate in to try and cure me of my cure um like help me with my absolute inability to communicate")

2. Performing poetry—writing and performing it live on stage—was a terrifying experience for her. (Verbatim: "you have to write it and then you can like act it out... so it's it is scary")

3. She pushes herself to do things she doesn’t want to do in order to grow personally. (Verbatim: "i always force myself into doing things i don't want to do per se to help me as a person in the long run")

4. She does not want to live with regret and is motivated by her parents’ constant expressions of unfulfilled potential. (Verbatim: "i grew up with parents that complained every day to me about how much potential they have... i don't want to look back in life and regret not trying")

5. She considers herself very ambitious but sometimes wishes she could just enjoy life without that drive. (Verbatim: "i'm a very ambitious person but... i wish i could just enjoy things without being ambitious")

6. Her work ethic is all-or-nothing: she is either completely unproductive or intensely productive. (Verbatim: "i'm actually a zero or 100 kind of productive kind of person... there's no in between")

7. She struggled with self-worth in college, believing she was lazier and less productive than others. (Verbatim: "i remember going through like college and stuff thinking wow everybody in life is so much more productive than me")

8. She was raised to believe she must always try her hardest, which contributed to her pressure to be constantly productive. (Verbatim: "i was raised to be like you must always try your hardest always and five ever or else")

9. She believes it’s okay to rest and that being lazy isn’t inherently bad. (Verbatim: "it's okay to chill it's okay to chill it's completely okay to chill")

10. Her debut as a VTuber was funded by a generous supporter she refers to as "my queen." (Verbatim: "my debut funds all from my queen they removed attaching a gift") [end of text]



